date-released: 2026-11-17
version: "1.1"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24250555
keywords:
  - cosmology
  - dark energy
  - interacting dark energy
  - interacting vacuum
  - DESI DR2
  - causal sets
  - N-body simulation
abstract: >-
  Spacetime as a causal graph of events: events create space, masses absorb it. This replaces dark energy with a
  source–sink interacting-vacuum model, which fits Planck 2018, DESI DR2 and supernova data better than ΛCDM
  (nominal 2.9–3.6 sigma) with one parameter fewer than w0wa, and predicts a line in the (w0, wa) plane.
